#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1731f4d0-2e00-51db-8ba8-df32c1c91bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263220} {:answer/id #uuid "35d5240f-4de5-5ab2-a31d-42037cfc6435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263475} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd1c6fb-594a-5b00-aa29-c8f0422c862c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264196} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b6c187-e4d1-55f9-ab48-a635363b3fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 16 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264403} {:answer/id #uuid "a59536c8-b0af-533f-8581-64006b7db377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264419}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263220} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd10dcce-5af6-5c25-bba5-38fc7025e371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "12adb9aa-d0f5-5652-8be9-e0603eaa1767" :question/math-academy-id "q-130136" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\cdot 1 & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1297b425-ab85-5bba-90d9-0aa321868ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263175} {:answer/id #uuid "3c0c371e-e1b3-52d8-84c6-a9a17f03d267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -15 \\\\ -16 & 20 \\\\ 8 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263534} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e8ab17-e45c-523a-a19c-a71e31ef33d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264584} {:answer/id #uuid "c36d4eae-a73f-53be-a310-030402b0ab31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264705} {:answer/id #uuid "d6eeee6e-2309-557d-bba3-b9d1577e7b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -15 \\\\ 8 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264871}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264584} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc268ea8-08d4-59b5-9560-41a3fd652f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "60c63572-fb04-5890-b3cf-3b16c8ce9cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130230" :question/problem "Find $ST$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$T=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $T$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $S$ and $2$ rows in $T$, so the product is undefined:\n\n$$\n{S}_{3\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{2\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255676dd-836e-5694-abf7-d5d8904ac9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263324} {:answer/id #uuid "2eda70ee-d361-5fce-9c20-c0b3d369e65a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263395} {:answer/id #uuid "b5361b1e-013d-5ce9-82f8-9cb252305b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "204" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264563} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ee1395-9652-5dad-99e0-df830e63634f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "220" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264890} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf0bcdb-ba33-5e2c-8a4d-88e00d25e056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265049}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263395} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab2e233-dfa3-53c1-8cbc-d36565b65180" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e431c517-0c91-5e86-97df-a91a6c031bdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-130484" :question/problem "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ find $det(Q).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=det\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =(4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-1))\\cdot (3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(-20)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =240.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fa62577-bf02-528f-b5ee-d1ce68202a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263827} {:answer/id #uuid "81b64480-8370-5e1a-bb30-61453b8fa4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264116} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc16a3a-5ddb-5094-8b95-277a446eb56b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264668} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7dacc0-93af-56e6-b8c2-fae50d4916ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264815} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6968e9-07fe-5033-9d69-52f737ed4fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263827} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4a12c3-6e0d-53f6-87cb-f0e7fedfe741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b687921-dfc7-598f-bc29-874fc54ba8a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130488" :question/problem "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle P=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ find $det(P).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(P)=det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =(3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2))\\cdot (8\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "702b6328-c32f-5527-b2ca-d3baaadb31ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263970} {:answer/id #uuid "7d75795f-2f71-5a1a-b8cc-d1f72992101b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-214" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264081} {:answer/id #uuid "9318164d-2060-5f48-886c-878e646e7c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264260} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0a2ee8-8586-50ff-ab69-638797faa787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "206" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264468} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a8cc04-1d7d-5562-8be8-65ee50e1bcc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264260} :answer-field/id #uuid "14d64a4d-a6ea-5c2c-a215-d5f4325e92b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6a11bbff-ca26-5c49-a8ab-b5946f4034f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130493" :question/problem "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(40-28)\\cdot (6-24) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-216.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c930cb-648d-5981-ad1b-ab3d1ac6543a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263312} {:answer/id #uuid "426f6f09-c48c-5c7c-8dde-97e1852580b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "206" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263586} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcde893-b9c7-5f37-b82a-366b325be86c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-236" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263674} {:answer/id #uuid "597beba5-ebc1-5875-b8bc-e7d0f915a765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263768} {:answer/id #uuid "84f97719-93d5-5bc8-bb1d-4514159fc0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264143} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be5b7b1-6bce-50a0-9ce6-981e62f75674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "315e2903-a515-5453-992e-2f5084f6607a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130497" :question/problem "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ find $det(C).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(8-18)\\cdot (36-10) \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =-260.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14df6deb-d3ee-5e1a-ad59-ff7cc32a5d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263194} {:answer/id #uuid "5cad807e-0569-5ff3-9e40-730b8b912410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263801} {:answer/id #uuid "79d24e48-d809-52e3-ad2f-fd1e75e9882a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264056} {:answer/id #uuid "aac71a88-0dd8-5c6f-afdc-8df09b432ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264462} {:answer/id #uuid "ed152b32-61af-5f9e-b9dd-61f70984cef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263194} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f7c60c4-fc52-503f-8ef4-67b53122d11d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "42eb872e-48fc-5f57-9397-6ecc0f021c29" :question/math-academy-id "q-130529" :question/problem "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+1(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2(-12+2)+(9-5)+(-6+20) \\\\  & =20+4+14 \\\\  & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=\\frac{1}{38}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "261340b2-1a0d-59dd-8b7b-76c4f7bfb121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263331} {:answer/id #uuid "3823e286-9476-5d05-a64b-0bd2a3d821f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=-1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263509} {:answer/id #uuid "6457994c-cd91-5a4c-915f-080f701162d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-5,\\,c=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263869} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7ea0e9-94d6-53d4-928a-c09488c89e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264456} {:answer/id #uuid "fa260fff-d100-5b94-a5b3-239f605d176d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-7,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263331} :answer-field/id #uuid "a814f1c0-7e30-52d3-b5a0-1628f163bffe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "585d1fdd-e4b6-5cfa-bfaf-54e4bf0c7de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130535" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+z &=1 \\\\ -x-3y+9z &=-2 \\\\ 4x-7y-z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & c \\\\ -1 & b & 9 \\\\ a & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b6213e-6630-5cbc-a2be-bba26537e9d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263842} {:answer/id #uuid "98683e89-44c4-5b63-a6a0-5143070e1a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=8,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264311} {:answer/id #uuid "a16f2ca2-4f2e-5acc-9b55-06d4bbfa6420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=8,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264374} {:answer/id #uuid "dc08dfd2-1ae1-53cb-adad-40873d7ac878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264916} {:answer/id #uuid "f9db3e03-47ba-53e0-8851-1e7f8c0aa7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265185} :answer-field/id #uuid "21ecd5d5-730f-53a8-b7fd-5892a28e6ac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "718180b1-bf73-575f-add7-0f6c8d9bba0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130536" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z &=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z &=1 \\\\ -6y+9z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z &=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z &=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04724195-4099-5efd-b607-d0a6ec716d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263041} {:answer/id #uuid "380da7e9-21d4-5706-85a2-87915110a7ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=5,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263505} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6ee337-2032-500b-8abc-6c320f482b06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263797} {:answer/id #uuid "8e82e001-fb77-5f38-9119-eb4019601441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=1,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264219} {:answer/id #uuid "bb46b3af-c697-5f07-8ba2-d5f423b58e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-7,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264628}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263797} :answer-field/id #uuid "2addae70-3713-5e28-bf38-96a976994060" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6babd892-4ff5-50c6-9630-e42df64db024" :question/math-academy-id "q-130562" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z-7x-5 &=0 \\\\ 4y-x-3z-2 &=0 \\\\ 2y+x-8 &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & a \\\\ b & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z &=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z &=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a96a6f2b-900e-5634-9638-19c6ba6bffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439527} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1afda0-1dac-5620-821a-ad4de506b094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/va